    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.align\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nSee reproduction.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. create `/tmp/repro.lua`, and execute `NVIM_APPNAME=repro nvim -u /tmp/repro.lua test.txt`:\n```lua\nvim.opt.cmdheight = 0\n\nrequire(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable({\n\tenable = true,\n\tmsg = { targets = \"cmd\" },\n})\n\nvim.pack.add({ \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\" }, { confirm = false })\n\nrequire(\"mini.align\").setup({})\n```\n3. create test content:\n```\nasd=asd\na=a\n```\n5. `Vjj` to select 2 lines\n6. press `gA`\n7. press `s=`\n8. press `Enter` to preview step7\n9. press `Enter` to apply，the cursor will jump into ui2 window, but not accept the adjusted result, the final result:\n\n<img width=\"1406\" height=\"499\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b500b84-0528-4421-adc6-5d5823feb89d\" />\n\n1. set `cmdheight=1` can work as expect\n2. without `ui2` can also wok as expect\n3. set `ui2` with `targets=\"msg\"` can also work as expect\n\n**To be honest, I'm not sure if this counts as a bug?**\n\n**Finally, thanks for your amazing plugin**",
